// spec: LEX-033
//
// A literal outside the 32-bit range is refused where it is READ.  It used to
// wrap: '2147483648' was the integer -2147483648 and '99999999999999' was
// 276447231 -- a value the source states plainly, silently replaced by a
// different one.
//
// ⚠️ 2147483647 is the largest that is accepted, and conformance/0013 pins it.
// There is no negative literal [LEX-019], so '-2147483648' is the unary minus
// applied to 2147483648 -- which means the most negative Integer cannot be
// written as a literal at all.  That is the same gap C has.

WriteLn (2147483648);
